meta {
  name: 50 Verify - Communications
  type: http
  seq: 20
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/communications?page=1&limit=25
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  ✅ VERIFY. Lists the tenant's CommunicationLog rows (most recent first). Each
  triggered notification created a row per deliverable channel; for EMAIL the
  resolved HTML is stored verbatim in the `body` field, so you can read every
  `label: value` line and confirm which tags resolved (and which are correctly
  blank — password, and phlebo_detail unless it was a home-visit order).

  The row is created even if the outbound Exchange gateway is not configured
  (status stays PENDING), so this works for pure tag verification. WhatsApp rows
  instead carry a positional `templateParams` array.

  Tip: eyeball the newest 5 rows — one each for create-order, partial payment,
  complete payment, report published, order completed.
}
